   "why": "After an outside review: Cerebras (AI chips, listed May 2026) was missing; Teradyne (chip testing), Celestica (AI networking and server hardware) and Quanta Services (grid and data-center power construction) fill infrastructure gaps. Dropped SoundHound and C3.ai (record closes from before the AI cycle), Applied Digital (Data centers keeps Equinix and Digital Realty) and Dell (Celestica covers AI hardware). Also added Tesla (a top AIQ holding whose value rests largely on self-driving and robots) and Oklo (nuclear power for data centers); dropped AppLovin (ad tech, the weakest AI link) and Western Digital (Seagate and Sandisk cover storage). Considered and left out: Apple (AI a small part of the business), NextEra (broad utility), Caterpillar (construction equipment), Adobe, Salesforce and Snowflake (record closes from 2021–24; a possible future 'disrupted by AI' group)."
